# __PROJECT_NAME__

Standard FPGA project scaffold for **__VENDOR__**. Project-specific device, clocks, resets, interfaces, constraints, and acceptance evidence must be recorded in this repository before implementation or sign-off.

## One-click entry points

- `project/script/run.bat`: refreshes file lists, runs preflight, then invokes the selected build adapter.
- `simulation/script/run.bat`: refreshes file lists, runs preflight, then invokes the selected simulation adapter.
- `linter/script/run.bat`: refreshes file lists, runs preflight, then invokes the configured lint tool.

The visible `script/` directories contain only the user-facing batch entry point, settings, canonical lists, and optional Tcl/do files. PowerShell helpers are isolated under each `script/ai_run/`; users do not need to invoke them directly.

Copy `project/script/toolchain.local.psd1.example` to the ignored `toolchain.local.psd1`, then set exact installed executable paths and confirmed arguments. A missing tool, vendor library, source, case, or project marker returns `UNVERIFIED`; it is not silently replaced.

Generated process files belong only under `codex_out/`. Release candidates are promoted explicitly to `release/output/` after project-defined review.

## Project structure

```text
document/
project/{rtl,sdc,par,script/{ai_run}}/
simulation/{tb/case,script/{ai_run}}/
linter/script/{ai_run}/
release/output/
codex_out/
```

Optional `project/ip`, `linter/lint_bb`, and `release/golden` directories are created only when requested by the scaffold command.

These canonical names are fixed for generated projects. Do not create numbered standard directories such as `project2`, `par2`, or `script2`.
